    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1152">

                <pb facs="1172" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/44a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-04T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 4, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2658. Please ascertain from Mr. Hoover
                    what arrangements, if any, he has made with the Central powers looking to
                    rendering relief to Serbia and Poland. Please telegraph reply as soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
